Cline, https://github.com/cline/cline, Copyright Cline Bot Inc., Apache License 2.0.
Cline itself is not stored in this repository. The build fetches it from upstream at the commit pinned in
engine/cline/lock.toml (tag cli-v3.0.71, commit 1a5c3f84e0933268a9dba14a55a6383a6578414d), checks it, and applies the
patches below. One part of this repository derives from Cline and keeps its license, and the worker image also carries two Cline
sources that are fetched at build and not stored here:

1. engine/cline/patches/ (the series and, under patches/tdd/, the test-only patches). These are git format-patch files that
   change Cline source. They carry lines of Cline's source as context and as changed code. The lines taken from Cline stay
   under the Apache License 2.0. The lines this project wrote are MIT-0.

2. The goal plugin of the Cline project (https://github.com/cline/plugins, plugins/goal/index.ts, commit
   96bde661f630ec23c1ce0cd86a2361a9959ef65a) and createTool of the Cline SDK (https://github.com/cline/cline,
   sdk/packages/shared/src/tools/create.ts, tag cli-v3.0.71, commit 1a5c3f84e0933268a9dba14a55a6383a6578414d). Apache License 2.0, the same
   licence text in both repositories. Neither is stored in this repository. The image build fetches both at the pins of
   engine/sources/goal-plugin.toml, bundles them with two small stand-ins we wrote (engine/sources/recipes/goal-plugin/) into the goal plugin
   folder of the worker image, and checks the five files against engine/plugins/lock.json. The folder carries the licence text and a notice
   that says what was changed, and the worker image carries the licence text and this file under /opt/harness/licenses/.

